        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0467" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg405"/>

                <head>No. 253.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Comly to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-07-08"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 8, 1878</date>.
                        (Received July 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 44.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit intelligence
                    of a change of ministry in the Hawaiian Government, His Majesty having demanded
                    the resignation of his former ministers. The new ministry is as follows:</p>
                <p>S. G. Wilder, minister of the interior, vice J. Mott Smith, resigned.</p>
                <p>J. M. Kapena, minister of foreign affairs, vice H. A. Peirce, resigned.</p>
                <p>Simon K. Kaai, minister of finance, vice J. M. Kapena, transferred.</p>
                <p>Edw. Preston, attorney-general, vice Alfred S. Hartwell, resigned.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES M. COMLY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
